# Ancient Cornucopia: "you may gain 1 life ... Do this only once each turn." The turn is used up only by actually gaining life
# (CR 603.2h: it "triggers only if its source's controller has not yet taken the indicated action that turn"). On turn 3 Bot1
# casts two Lightning Bolts, each red: for the first it declines (no life), so the second still triggers it and Bot1 accepts and
# gains 1. Life 20 + 1 = 21, and Bot2 takes 6 (to 14).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Ancient Cornucopia
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancient Cornucopia.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Decline
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Cornucopia.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot2.Life = 14
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt
